-- expect: 5:1: `(+)` has its machine cases at the integer widths (the host's instructions): a case at `i64` would overlap them
-- An operator's family has the host's instruction as its case at each integer width (SPEC §36); a
-- program's case at one would be a second case at that type.

poly (+) at i64 = a

main -> i64 = i64[1] + i64[2]
